/ amend must not read the slot it just freed.  kamendi4v/kamendi4d mutate an
/ unshared target in place (r-gated), and they free the old slot before
/ building the new value -- so a value that can REACH the target (the live
/ tree via .`, a fresh list holding the target, the target itself) used to
/ walk back into the half-updated target and read freed memory (AFL sig 11
/ in dcp, 2026-07-13).  amend_yalias snapshots such a value up front.

